From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:53:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Start a tile's video delay with its selection

A grid tile selected with an animation started its video only at the
end of its 250 ms zoom, so the video's delay came after it: a card's
video showed a quarter of a second later than the delay said, even with
no zoom at all. The video is started with the selection (it is sized
for the selected tile already and shows after its delay).
---
 es-core/src/components/GridTileComponent.cpp | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/es-core/src/components/GridTileComponent.cpp b/es-core/src/components/GridTileComponent.cpp
index ba0dda42..23f39186 100644
--- a/es-core/src/components/GridTileComponent.cpp
+++ b/es-core/src/components/GridTileComponent.cpp
@@ -1317,11 +1317,15 @@ void GridTileComponent::setSelected(bool selected, bool allowAnimation, Vector3f
 			};
 
 			cancelAnimation(3);
-			setAnimation(new LambdaAnimation(func, 250), 0, [this, startsVideo] {
+
+			// The video's own delay starts with the selection, not after the zoom: it is sized for the selected
+			// tile already, and shows only after its delay
+			if (startsVideo)
+				startVideo();
+
+			setAnimation(new LambdaAnimation(func, 250), 0, [this] {
 				this->setSelectedZoom(1);
 				mAnimPosition = Vector3f(0, 0, 0);
-				if (startsVideo)
-					startVideo();
 			}, false, 3);
 		}
 	}
